        <body>
            <div xml:id="d523-a1">

                <pb facs="0857" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg841"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">WFM T–10/1</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">(Supplement)</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Views of the Embassy in London on Probable British
                        Attitudes on Subjects To Be Discussed in the Washington Foreign Ministers’
                        Meetings</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">korea (if no armistice)</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The chief concern of the British is that the US may renew full-scale military
                    effort. They hope for an effective stalemate in absence of <pb facs="0858"
                        n="842" xml:id="pg842"/> major air intervention, in which case they would
                    probably be prepared to accept full-scale war with China, perhaps leading to
                    general war.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
